---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CallBand from '../../components/CallBand.astro';
---
<Base title="Sample Kept Memo" description="What a bkept client receives with every monthly close: a one-page, plain-English summary of the month. Sample with invented figures.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero hero-center">
      <span class="eyebrow boxed">What to Expect</span>
      <h1>A Sample <span class="gold-text">Kept Memo.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Every monthly close comes with one page like this. The business and figures below are invented; real memos stay between us and the client.</p>
    </section>

    <article class="memo">
      <div class="memo-head">
        <div>
          <span class="logo">bkept.</span>
          <div class="muted">The Kept Memo · September 2026</div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align:right;">
          <span class="sample-flag">Sample</span>
          <div class="muted" style="margin-top:6px;">Prepared for: a 12-person design studio<br />Books closed: October 9</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p><strong>The month in one line:</strong> Your best revenue month this year and a healthy profit, but cash fell because two large clients are paying late.</p>

      <h2>The Numbers</h2>
      <table class="memo-table">
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>September</th><th>August</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Revenue</td><td>$142,300</td><td>$128,900</td><td>+10.4%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gross margin</td><td>61.0%</td><td>62.5%</td><td>−1.5 pts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Net income</td><td>$15,600</td><td>$9,800</td><td>+$5,800</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cash on hand</td><td>$188,400</td><td>$201,700</td><td>−$13,300</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Owed to you, over 60 days</td><td>$38,500</td><td>$6,200</td><td>+$32,300</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>What Changed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Two new retainer clients started, adding $11,000 a month in recurring revenue.</li>
        <li>Profit rose even though contractor costs grew, because rent and software were flat.</li>
        <li>Cash went down while profit went up. The gap is two invoices totaling $38,500, now more than 60 days old.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What to Watch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contractor costs</strong> reached 22% of revenue, up from 18% in the spring. Fine for a busy quarter; worth a look if it holds.</li>
        <li><strong>Cash low point:</strong> the 13-week forecast dips to about $96,000 in mid-November, when the quarterly estimated tax and the annual insurance renewal land in the same week.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Decisions for You</h2>
      <div class="decision"><strong>1. Late invoices.</strong> Should we send a firm reminder on the two overdue invoices this week, or would you rather call the clients first?</div>
      <div class="decision"><strong>2. Deposits.</strong> Consider a 50% deposit on new projects over $20,000. It would have kept roughly $19,000 more cash in the bank this month.</div>
      <div class="decision"><strong>3. Duplicate software.</strong> You pay for two project management tools ($9,600 a year combined). Keep one and we will cancel the other before it renews on November 1.</div>

      <h2>Open Items</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Three card charges need a receipt (list sent with this memo). Please reply by the 5th of next month.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:30px;">Full P&amp;L, Balance Sheet and Cash Flow Statement attached. We'll walk through all of this at your monthly review.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <CallBand title="Want this every month?" text="A 20-minute call with Tom. Bring whatever you need help with, and we will shape the engagement around it." />
</Base>
